---
term: Independent formation
aka:
  - Formation ex natura
section: life-cycle
order: 20
definition: The creation of a charter without a parent, so that the charter exists *ex natura*, directly under the [[Natural Charter]].
seeAlso:
  - charter-formation
  - highest-human-charter
  - status
---
A charter formed this way has no contract period, because it has no second party to make a contract with or to be admitted into. It relates to every party outside it through the [[status|statuses]] that its own articles assign.

Many charters can exist ex natura at once. Each is the top of its own structure until it joins a parent through [[admission]] or helps form one through [[conversion]].

Whether a charter's first articles need ratification by its members, expire after a set period, or neither, is a choice for each charter's design.
